#. meta description
#: about.html
msgid ""
"Duct began as one person's fix for tools that would not talk to each other. It went open source because an agent that reads your business should be readable."
msgstr "Duct 最初是一个人为了解决工具之间无法互通的问题而创建的。它之所以开源，是因为一个读取你业务的智能体应该是可读的。"

#: about.html
msgid ""
"Duct is MIT licensed, on your own keys or your ChatGPT plan. Star the repo if it is useful, open an issue if it is not."
msgstr "Duct 采用 MIT 许可，使用你自己的密钥或 ChatGPT 计划。如果它有用，请给仓库加星；如果没有用，请提出问题。"

#: about.html
msgid ""
"Duct reads across the tools you already run and answers the question none of them can answer alone: why did this move, and what do we do about it. Not another dashboard. Not another data warehouse project you will abandon in Q3. And when the answer is “pause that campaign” or “mark that GA4 event,” Duct can prepare the change and show you a preview. It cannot apply it. Only you can. That boundary lives in code, not in a prompt."
msgstr ""
"Duct 读取你已运行的工具，并回答它们都无法单独回答的问题：为什么会发生这种变化，我们该如何应对。它不是另一个仪表盘，也不是另一个你会在第三季度放弃的数据仓库项目。当答案是“暂停该广告系列”或“标记该 GA4 事件”时，Duct 可以准备变更并向你显示预览。它无法应用变更。只有你可以。这个界限存在于代码中，而不是在提示中。"

#: about.html
msgid ""
"Duct reads by default. When it can fix something, it prepares a change set, shows you a preview and a guardrail check, and waits. The agent can propose and inspect; it cannot approve or apply. That decision lives in code the model never sees, and rollback is part of the contract."
msgstr ""
"Duct 默认读取。当它可以修复某些问题时，它会准备一个变更集，向你显示预览和安全检查，然后等待。智能体可以提出和检查；它不能批准或应用。该决定存在于模型永远看不到的代码中，并且回滚是合同的一部分。"

#: about.html
msgid ""
"Each one reads across the twelve connected sources instead of one at a time, and when the answer is a change, it prepares the change and waits for you. Every connector and every prompt is in the repo, so this list is the list, not a roadmap."
msgstr "每个都读取十二个已连接的来源，而不是一次一个，当答案是变更时，它会准备变更并等待你。每个连接器和每个提示都在仓库中，所以这个列表就是列表，而不是路线图。"

#: about.html
msgid ""
"Every data source, every API call, every prompt, every piece of logic that generates a signal is <0>on GitHub</0>. Not documented and inspectable in principle. Actually there, actually readable, actually forkable."
msgstr ""
"每个数据源、每个 API 调用、每个提示、每个生成信号的逻辑片段都<0>在 GitHub 上</0>。不是原则上可文档化和可检查。而是实际存在、实际可读、实际可分叉。"

#: about.html
msgid ""
"Every one of those jobs had the same gap: the answer to “why did that number move” was never inside one tool, and somebody senior burned a morning every week carrying the numbers between tools by hand. Duct is the thing I wanted for that job, so I built it and made it MIT."
msgstr ""
"所有这些工作都有相同的空白：对“为什么那个数字变动了”的答案从未在一个工具中找到，而且每周都有高级人员花费一个上午手动在工具之间搬运数字。Duct 就是我为那项工作想要的东西，所以我构建了它并将其开源为 MIT 许可。"

#: about.html
msgid ""
"Every product team runs 8–12 tools. Each one sees a sliver. I got tired of being the integration layer between them, so I wrote one. Then I put it on GitHub under MIT, because a thing that reads your whole business has to be readable back."
msgstr ""
"每个产品团队都运行 8–12 个工具。每个工具都只看到一小部分。我厌倦了充当它们之间的集成层，所以我写了一个。然后我把它放在 GitHub 上，采用 MIT 许可，因为一个读取你整个业务的东西必须是可读的。"

#: about.html
msgid "FONS. The spring, before anything has run. The app’s front door."
msgstr "FONS。泉水，在任何运行之前。应用的入口。"

