msgid "Privacy Policy"
msgstr "隐私政策"

#: about.html
msgid ""
"Product manager and engineer. Most of my career has gone into building products from scratch and scaling them at fin-tech and ed-tech companies, a lot of it AI and ML systems serving millions of users. Open-source contributor throughout."
msgstr ""
"产品经理兼工程师。我的职业生涯大部分时间都在从零开始构建产品，并在金融科技和教育科技公司将其规模化，其中很多是服务数百万用户的 AI 和 ML 系统。一直以来都是开源贡献者。"

#: about.html
msgid ""
"Read access to your ads, analytics and revenue is a lot to hand a tool, and a lot more to hand a tool built by one person. I cannot ask for that trust; I can show the code. Every prompt, every API call and the approval gate itself are in the repository under MIT. Download the app and I run the service for you; clone it and nothing touches me. It is free with your own keys, and stays that way. A paid plan will bundle the models later, for teams that would rather hold no keys at all. <0>What runs where, and what will cost money</0> has its own page."
msgstr ""
"授予一个工具读取你的广告、分析和收入的权限是一件大事，而授予一个由一个人构建的工具更是如此。我不能要求这种信任；我可以展示代码。每个提示、每个 API 调用以及批准门本身都在 MIT 许可下的仓库中。下载应用，我为你运行服务；克隆它，则与我无关。使用你自己的密钥是免费的，并且会一直如此。付费计划稍后会捆绑模型，适用于那些不想持有任何密钥的团队。<0>什么在哪里运行，以及什么会收费</0>有单独的页面。"

#: about.html
msgid "Read it, run it, <0>break it.</0>"
msgstr "阅读它，运行它，<0>打破它。</0>"

